course: dictionary
lesson: 6695
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Occupy is one of these words. «The table occupies two square metres» means the table takes up that much space, so occupy means to fill a space.
explain: «Japan occupied Manchuria in 1931» means something different. Here occupy means taking control of a place, often by force, as an army does. Ask yourself: who is doing what, and to what place? The words around occupy are the clues.
explain: Occupy can also mean to keep busy. A sign on a toilet door that says «occupied» means someone is inside. If you are occupied with homework, your time is full of homework. Try each meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Occupy is a verb. Its other forms are occupies, occupied and occupying.
fact: To occupy a room or building means to live in it or use it.
fact: To occupy someone's time means to fill it or keep them busy.
fact: To occupy a place means to take control of it by force, as an army can.
fact: To occupy a job or position means to have it.
exercise: «The table occupies two square metres of the room.» What does occupies mean here? | Keeps busy | *Takes up | Is in charge of | Lives in
exercise: «Japan occupied Manchuria in 1931.» What does occupied mean here? | *Took control of the place by force | Had a job there | Filled the time with games | Lived in peacefully as a guest
exercise: A sign on a toilet door says «occupied». What does it tell you? | The toilet is broken | Nobody is allowed in | *Someone is inside | The door is painted
test:  Dad has been occupied all morning with the garden. What does occupied mean? | Asleep | *Kept busy | Lost | Very angry
test: «She occupies the top job at the school.» What does occupies mean? | Leaves | *Has the position | Cleans | Climbs
exam: «The army occupied the town.» Which meaning fits best? | *Took control of the town by force | Lived in a tent outside the town | Filled the town with songs | Had lunch there
